<h2 class="bold" id="js-module-reference"><a class="underline reset-text-decoration" href="file#js-module-reference">JS Module Reference</a></h2>
<p>The JS Module is responsible for updating label text with the selected file name.</p>
<p>All elements matching <span class="code-wrapper code-container inline" style="background-color:hsl(230, 1%, 98%);color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><code class="code code--inline prism-code language-markup code-inline"><span class="token-line" style="color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><span class="token plain">input[type=&quot;file&quot;].file-input</span></span></code></span> selector with a unique <span class="code-wrapper code-container inline" style="background-color:hsl(230, 1%, 98%);color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><code class="code code--inline prism-code language-markup code-inline"><span class="token-line" style="color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><span class="token plain">name</span></span></code></span> attribute will be initialised automatically.</p>
<p><strong><span class="code-wrapper code-container inline" style="background-color:hsl(230, 1%, 98%);color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><code class="code code--inline prism-code language-markup code-inline"><span class="token-line" style="color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><span class="token plain">input[name]</span></span></code></span></strong> must be specified for the JS module to initialize.</p>
<h3 class="bold" id="custom-initialization"><a class="underline reset-text-decoration" href="file#custom-initialization">Custom initialization</a></h3>
